{"uid":"d188e03537edcfef","name":"test_reason_extraction_walks_a_nested_problem_body_to_the_innermost_string","fullName":"tests.test_browser_hub#test_reason_extraction_walks_a_nested_problem_body_to_the_innermost_string","historyId":"633960c411ec4f5406c0bfaef392c48e","time":{"start":1791957913952,"stop":1791957932223,"duration":18271},"description":"Task 069 (#155, requirement G.7): both the steer form's error branch\n    and `renderRetryNow`'s fallback used to stop at the first TRUTHY value\n    in their own `||` chain -- which, for a body nested one `detail` deeper\n    than either chain expected, is an OBJECT, and `String()` on an object\n    renders the literal text `[object Object]`. This is exactly the shape\n    the hub's own proxy produces when the run's live API answers a mutating\n    request with a problem document that itself carries a `detail` key\n    (`ui_server.py`'s `do_POST`: `{\"error\": ..., \"detail\": <engine body>}`,\n    and the engine's own body here is `{\"detail\": {\"title\": ..., \"detail\":\n    \"steering has no effect\"}}`) -- e.g. a run that finishes between the\n    browser's submit and the proxy's forward (#179's family).\n\n    Confirmed this node genuinely pins the defect: reverted `app.js` to the\n    pre-069 `||` chains (`git show HEAD:src/ralphd/cli/web/app.js` before\n    this commit) and re-ran this node solo -- both of the first two\n    assertions failed with the rendered text containing the literal\n    `[object Object]` instead of `steering has no effect`. Restored the fix\n    before this commit landed.\n\n    The rest of the node then re-drives the RETRY surface (the two share\n    one helper, already proven identical above by the nested-body checks)\n    against the three shapes that worked before this task and must keep\n    working: a flat `{error: ...}`, the 401 control-token body task 007\n    introduced (`{detail: {title, status, detail: \"mutating routes require\n    the control token\"}}`), and a body with no string anywhere, which must\n    still fall back to the numeric status. The retry proxy passes the\n    engine's body through verbatim with no added wrapper key (unlike the\n    steer proxy, which always adds its own top-level `error` string), so\n    driving these three through retry tests the helper against exactly the\n    named shape with nothing else in play.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 069 (#155, requirement G.7): both the steer form's error branch<br />\nand <code>renderRetryNow</code>'s fallback used to stop at the first TRUTHY value<br />\nin their own <code>||</code> chain -- which, for a body nested one <code>detail</code> deeper<br />\nthan either chain expected, is an OBJECT, and <code>String()</code> on an object<br />\nrenders the literal text <code>[object Object]</code>. This is exactly the shape<br />\nthe hub's own proxy produces when the run's live API answers a mutating<br />\nrequest with a problem document that itself carries a <code>detail</code> key<br />\n(<code>ui_server.py</code>'s <code>do_POST</code>: <code>{&quot;error&quot;: ..., &quot;detail&quot;: &lt;engine body&gt;}</code>,<br />\nand the engine's own body here is <code>{&quot;detail&quot;: {&quot;title&quot;: ..., &quot;detail&quot;: &quot;steering has no effect&quot;}}</code>) -- e.g. a run that finishes between the<br />\nbrowser's submit and the proxy's forward (#179's family).</p>\n<pre><code>Confirmed this node genuinely pins the defect: reverted `app.js` to the\npre-069 `||` chains (`git show HEAD:src/ralphd/cli/web/app.js` before\nthis commit) and re-ran this node solo -- both of the first two\nassertions failed with the rendered text containing the literal\n`[object Object]` instead of `steering has no effect`. Restored the fix\nbefore this commit landed.\n\nThe rest of the node then re-drives the RETRY surface (the two share\none helper, already proven identical above by the nested-body checks)\nagainst the three shapes that worked before this task and must keep\nworking: a flat `{error: ...}`, the 401 control-token body task 007\nintroduced (`{detail: {title, status, detail: &quot;mutating routes require\nthe control token&quot;}}`), and a body with no string anywhere, which must\nstill fall back to the numeric status. The retry proxy passes the\nengine's body through verbatim with no added wrapper key (unlike the\nsteer proxy, which always adds its own top-level `error` string), so\ndriving these three through retry tests the helper against exactly the\nnamed shape with nothing else in play.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791957833013,"stop":1791957833014,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791957833014,"stop":1791957833014,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791957913949,"stop":1791957913949,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791957913949,"stop":1791957913950,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791957913950,"stop":1791957913951,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"ha